course: dictionary
lesson: 6607
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, the words around them, tells you which meaning the writer wants. Noodle is a good example: it can be food, a head, or a floating tube.
explain: «In swimming lessons, children use pool noodles to help them float.» The word pool is the clue. A pool noodle is a long, soft foam tube, not something you eat.
explain: «Use your noodle» is an informal phrase. It means think, not cook. Always ask: what meaning fits here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A noodle is a long, thin strip of dough made from flour, water and sometimes egg, cooked in boiling water or soup.
fact: Informally, your noodle is your head or brain, so «use your noodle» means think carefully.
fact: A pool noodle is a long, soft foam tube used to help you float in water.
fact: «chángshòumiàn» are longevity noodles eaten on birthdays, especially grandparents' birthdays, because long noodles mean long life.
exercise: «A 4,000-year-old bowl of millet noodles was found at Lajia in China.» What are noodles here? | A soft toy for the bath | A hard metal tool | A kind of bird | *Long, thin strips of dough cooked in water
exercise: Sam says, «Use your noodle before you guess.» What does use your noodle mean? | Float on your back | Cook a bowl of soup | *Think carefully | Put on a hat
exercise: «chángshòumiàn» are longevity noodles eaten on birthdays. Why are long noodles eaten? | Because they are cut into short pieces | Because they are the cheapest food | Because they help you float | *Because long noodles mean long life
test: Lena says, «I need to use my noodle to solve this puzzle.» What does noodle mean? | *Your head or brain | A foam tube for floating | A bowl of soup | A kind of bread
test: Which sentence uses noodle to mean food? | Use your noodle and think it through | *Everyone slurped their noodle soup at the table | Dad reached for his noodle in the cupboard | The pool noodle floated on the water
exam: «A 4,000-year-old bowl of millet noodles was found in China.» What does this tell you about noodles? | Noodles were invented last week | Noodles only come from Italy | *People have been eating noodles for thousands of years | Noodles are a kind of animal
